  "question": {
    "text": "A fully charged capacitor has a capacitance ' $C$ ' it is discharged through a small coil of resistance wire embedded in a thermally insulated block of specific heat capacity ' $s$ ' and mass ' $\\mathrm{m}$ '. If the temperature of the block is raised by ' $\\Delta \\mathrm{T}$ '. The potential difference $V$ across the capacitance is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "saOqN",
      "text": "\n$\\sqrt{\\frac{2 m C \\Delta T}{s}}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "97MXk",
      "text": "\n$\\frac{\\mathrm{mC} \\Delta \\mathrm{T}}{\\mathrm{s}}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ba4JU",
      "text": "\n$\\frac{\\mathrm{ms} \\Delta \\mathrm{T}}{\\mathrm{c}}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "kBVmt",
      "text": "\n$\\sqrt{\\frac{2 m s \\Delta T}{C}}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Dimensionally only $4^{\\text {th }}$ option is correct.",
